{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mr5l0el0i0k","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"EWM run sixteen goal discovery exploration and model trusted fast path design","summary":"Run 15 left the recalled ls20 model live-perfect (1.0, 18/18) but two blockers: agent never SEEN a win (is_win vacuously False, no banked level boundary) and throughput was 17 actions in 25 min (minutes per decide, because every EXECUTE batch runs a reflect LLM call and plans are short with no goal). Fix in agent.py + planner.py: (1) GOAL DISCOVERY mode — when a program is adopted with high live confidence but is_win never fires and no plan is found, plan FRONTIER EXPLORATION on CPU via planner.explore_frontier (BFS over the model reachable-state graph maximizing NEW player-cell coverage), execute in long budget-guarded batches, watch every real transition for a level or score boundary (env level counter increment or score jump / level_transition stop_reason); on first boundary capture the transition, record a game-scoped goal note (title 'game <id> level <n> goal evidence') via kb.write_goal_evidence, and re-derive is_win as a goal-contact predicate over the captured player position. (2) MODEL-TRUSTED FAST PATH — while a rolling window of live predictions all pass, skip the reflect LLM call (reflection log-only; suite still appends every transition) and extend planned batch length to the budget-guard cap; ANY expect-mismatch instantly restores full decide/reflect cadence and normal batch sizes. Telemetry: coverage_pct, actions_per_minute, llm_calls_per_action. Frontier explorer and fast path are pure/deterministic and unit-tested against the toy game's real level transition.","category":null,"tags":[],"created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-07-03T23:45:54.900Z","vec":[-0.01790395751595497,-0.00423824368044734,-0.053752798587083817,0.028656726703047752,0.09626001864671707,-0.05970722809433937,-0.0640987679362297,0.05004015937447548,-0.03789961338043213,0.07856743782758713,-0.008039376